reports/qa/US-03-qa-report.md:58:The initial broad browser run used Angular `ng serve`, which returned its SPA fallback for two unmatched `/api/form-configurations` and `/api/plans` requests that the existing tests expect to return 404. The full suite then passed 22/22 against the isolated static Compose deployment, which confirmed the production-style API responses. The dedicated US-03 terms API boundary test also passed against Strapi for its generated-route, query and method cases.
reports/qa/US-03-qa-report.md:64:## Approved copy revision re-verification, 2026-11-22
reports/qa/US-03-qa-report.md:66:The QA flow now checks that the retired fictitious-data introduction and identity-number hint are absent from Details; Summary exposes the `Resultado de prueba` group and `Pagar` action without the former demonstration heading, no-real-charge sentence, or `Simular pago` action; and the approved receipt contains no country name or standalone no-charge sentence. These are copy acceptance checks, not a new QA defect. The Colombia and Chile full quote flows each exercised rejection, retry with preserved owner and selected plan, approval, and reload of the same receipt. Both passed on the refreshed local Compose app at `127.0.0.1:8080`. The isolated terms API, direct-route prerequisite, and interrupted-check reload tests also passed in the same five-test run.
reports/qa/US-03-qa-report.md:68:During the first follow-up attempt, the new Details copy checks completed, but the CO flow timed out because the QA helper expected the former `Ejemplo Motor` option while the refreshed CO seed offers `Mazda` and `Chevrolet`. The test helper now selects the first configured brand option. This was test fixture drift, not an application defect. The focused rerun passed 2/2 country flows, then the complete dedicated suite passed 5/5. `prettier --check e2e/us03-qa.spec.ts` passed before the reruns.
reports/qa/US-03-qa-report.md:72:The US-03 behavior passed dedicated browser, CMS integration, unit and full cross-story browser coverage. US03-QA-01 is resolved with evidence. No blocking implementation defect was reproduced. Native screen-reader and operating-system high-contrast checks remain unverified.
